From 3e998b532181021996d2f687950ccf58f95ba551 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HaoWang113 <18701975378@163.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:04:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [ckpt, rollout] fix: ship the vllm-ascend expert-loader patch
 in-tree and self-diagnose its absence

E2E run 3 hit the d8e3a872 fail-loud on the NPU machine: the expert
weight_loader guard fired at window open because the runtime vllm-ascend
install was still stock. Root cause of the non-transfer: the v2 patch file
lived untracked in tests/special_npu/, so neither git pull nor the exported
commit patches could carry it to the machine, and the machine-facing test
guide had no patch step at all.

- Track tests/special_npu/vllm_ascend_moe_online_update_0230rc1.patch
  (script artifacts in that dir are already tracked; only prose docs stay
  out) so the patch travels with the branch and commit-patch exports.
- Extend the weight_loader fail-loud to print the runtime host module
  path plus the exact grep that verifies the patch marker in THAT file,
  turning any recurrence into a ten-second diagnosis (also flags that
  reinstalling vllm-ascend wipes a patch applied inside site-packages).

Verified the guard itself is sound against a patched host: the check runs
before any verl-side flip, and the only rebinds on the 0.23.0rc1 stack are
the two process_weights_after_loading Parameter() assignments the patch
rewrites -- super(UnquantizedFusedMoEMethod, self) skips vllm core's
method into a no-op base, so no other path can drop the attribute.

Co-authored-by: GLM5.3 <noreply@zhipuai.com>
Signed-off-by: Hao Wang <wanghao232@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Chuan Zheng <zhengchuan@huawei.com>
